{"id": "y0572", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Erosion could lead to A, a change in the direction of a stream. This is because as soil and rock are worn away by water or wind, it can alter the course of rivers or streams over time. The other options, like ocean temperatures or weather patterns, are usually influenced by different factors such as climate change rather than erosion itself. As for plants and animals, er osion might actually reduce their habitat s, so an increase in them is not typically a direct result.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0580", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cellular respiration' s trash is a plant's treasure. When cells break down glucose for energy, they release carbon di oxide as a byproduct. Plants use this carbon dioxide during photosynthesis to make their own food, turning it into oxygen and glucose. So, what seems like waste to animals becomes valuable nutrient s for plants.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0588", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Butterflies don't have bar bs on their backs to sting. They are gentle creatures that feed on nectar and do not possess stinging ability like wasps or scorpions.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0596", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A dry cobble stone road is most likely to cause a driver to lose control. The uneven surface of cobble stones can make it difficult to steer smoothly and maintain traction, especially at higher speeds. While gravel roads are also less smooth than paved surfaces, they usually offer more predictable driving conditions compared to the irregular pattern s of cobblestones.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0604", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The most logical choice is D, turning on the ho se. Since the mud is still wet and track ing everywhere, using a hose would be the practical way to clean it up quickly. Getting a new child or yell ing at the mud doesn' t solve the problem, and asking the child to stop might not work if they're having fun. So turn ing on the ho se makes the most sense here.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0612", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A dog is more likely to shiver at 5 AM. That early morning hour often brings cooler temperatures and a quiet environment, which can make dogs feel chilly or anxious. Many dogs are awake then but not fully active, so they might shake off the cold or respond to subtle stress. While other times like 1 PM or 6 PM could also be cooler depending on location, 5 AM stands out as a prime time for shivering due to temperature drop and lack of activity.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 24, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y0620", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A nocturnal predator would most likely hunt at 3 a.m., as that is during the night when such animals are active.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
