{"id": "y1036", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So let's think about this. We know that the sun follows the inverse square law, meaning that its intensity drops off with the square of the distance from it. If Ju piter is roughly 5 AU away and Earth is at 1 AU, then the solar flux at Jupiter would be spread over an area that is 25 times larger than at Earth because 5 squared is 25. That means the light intensity there would be one-2 5th of what we get on Earth if the sun stayed the same. To make up for that distance, the sun would have to be 2 5 times brighter so that Europa receives the same amount of sunlight as we do on Earth. The answer is B, 25 times brighter.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 38, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1044", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C, pay-per-click. PPC involves advertisers bid ding on keywords to have their ads displayed when those terms are searched for, and they only pay when a user clicks on the ad. SEO focuses on organic ranking s without direct cost per click, while context ual advertising targets based on content context rather than keyword bidding.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
