{"id": "y1060", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So, persons who have work-related accidents tend to feel more dissatisfied with their work than accident- free workers. They also tend to be less likely to have had job promotions than accident- free workers. However, there isn't a direct correlation between having an accident and recent life stress or intelligence. The most accurate answer based on typical research findings is that they tend to feel more dissatisfied with their work and are less likely to get promoted. So, A and B would both be correct, but if you had to pick one, feeling more dissatisfied with their work is often the primary observation.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1068", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 22, "onset_chunk": 21, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So the correct statement about Engel' s law is option A. As income rises, the proportion of income spent on food declines. This is because as people earn more money, they tend to spend a smaller percentage of their income on basic needs like food and allocate more towards other expenses such as housing, entertainment, or savings.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
